            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <p>Running out of ad account balance and causing campaign interruptions is more common than you might think. Especially during scaling periods, a sudden ad pause can disrupt your conversion model, often requiring 3-5 days for recovery. Prevention is always better than remediation.</p>
<h2>Step 1: Define Alert Thresholds</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Primary Alert</strong>: Account Balance &lt; (Daily Budget × 3)</li>
<li><strong>Secondary Alert</strong>: Account Balance &lt; (Daily Budget × 1.5)</li>
<li><strong>Emergency Alert</strong>: Account Balance &lt; $500 (regardless of budget size)</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>For multi-account management, set individual thresholds per account rather than applying a uniform standard.</p>
</blockquote>
<h2>Step 2: Enable Native Platform Notifications</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Platform</th>
<th>Path</th>
<th>Notification Type</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Meta (Facebook)</strong></td>
<td>Business Settings → Payments → Alerts</td>
<td>Email + In-app</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Google Ads</strong></td>
<td>Tools → Billing → Alert preferences</td>
<td>Email + SMS</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>TikTok Ads</strong></td>
<td>Assets → Budget &amp; Schedule → Low balance alert</td>
<td>In-app notification</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Pinterest</strong></td>
<td>Ads → Billing → Spending limit alerts</td>
<td>Email only</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2>Step 3: Configure Third-Party Monitoring</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Spreadsheets with API integration</strong>: Pull data automatically and set threshold formulas</li>
<li><strong>Slack/Teams/Lark bots</strong>: Custom webhook alerts sent directly to your team channel</li>
<li><strong>Email routing</strong>: Create dedicated folders with mobile push notifications</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pre-Launch / Weekly Checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Check all account balances</li>
<li>[ ] Verify balance for active campaigns specifically</li>
<li>[ ] Test alert delivery (send a test notification)</li>
<li>[ ] Confirm payment methods are active</li>
<li>[ ] Know platform processing times (credit card vs. wire transfer)</li>
<li>[ ] Backup accounts pre-funded if possible</li>
<li>[ ] Assign balance monitoring to team on-call schedule</li>
</ul>
<h2>Emergency Protocols</h2>
<h3>Scenario A: Balance drops at night or during holidays</h3>
<ul>
<li>Pre-fund low-balance accounts before off-hours</li>
<li>Set up auto-recharge rules where available</li>
<li>Ensure team member can access ad dashboard via mobile</li>
</ul>
<h3>Scenario B: Payment method fails</h3>
<ul>
<li>Verify backup payment methods are validated</li>
<li>Maintain contact with agency/agent for emergency top-ups</li>
<li>Temporarily reduce budgets on secondary campaigns for buffer time</li>
</ul>
<h3>Scenario C: Multiple accounts alert simultaneously</h3>
<ul>
<li>Prioritize 2-3 highest-ROI accounts</li>
<li>Pause lower-priority accounts until main accounts are funded</li>
<li>Use batch management tools for unified handling</li>
</ul>
<h2>Common Pitfalls</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Focusing on daily spend rate instead of total balance</strong>: Low daily spend doesn't mean sufficient total balance</li>
<li><strong>Setting only one alert level</strong>: Miss the optimal replenishment window</li>
<li><strong>No alert testing</strong>: Notifications blocked or filtered to spam</li>
<li><strong>Relying solely on manual checks</strong>: Highest risk during holidays and off-hours</li>
</ul>
<p>A solid balance alert system transforms your risk management from reactive firefighting to proactive prevention. Regular reviews of spending patterns and optimized top-up schedules free your team to focus on creative optimization and ROI improvement.</p>
